<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Guidelines for Formatting Test Cases</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Creating well-structured <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">test case descriptions</span> is crucial for ensuring the optimal performance of <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">LELANTE</span>’s LLM-based processing pipeline. Poorly written test cases can introduce <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ambiguity</span>, making it difficult for the model to interpret and execute the correct actions. For example, instead of saying <span id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Add category inside the Edit Category window"</span>, a clearer version would be <span id="A1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Add a new category named <span id="A1.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Elysium</span> from inside the Edit Category window"</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, test cases should be structured to provide only <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">essential details</span> while maintaining <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">precision</span>. If an action can be performed in multiple ways, only <span id="A1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">one method</span> should be specified, such as <span id="A1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Set call vibration as <span id="A1.p2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Basic call</span> in Call alerts and ringtones"</span> instead of just <span id="A1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Set call vibration as <span id="A1.p2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Basic call</span>"</span>. <span id="A1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unnecessary details</span> should be avoided when there is only <span id="A1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">one way</span> to complete a task. When necessary, <span id="A1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">explicit directions</span> should be provided to help locate options within the UI, such as clarifying that <span id="A1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Gallery settings are located in the drawer"</span>. Finally, test case descriptions should always include the <span id="A1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">final confirmation step</span> to prevent premature completion—an instruction like <span id="A1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Update Samsung account profile picture by taking a picture"</span> should be revised to <span id="A1.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Update Samsung account profile picture by taking a picture. Click <span id="A1.p2.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Done</span> to save"</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Prompt structure</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure accurate test execution, <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">LELANTE</span> employs a structured prompt shown below that guides the LLM in understanding the test case, evaluating prior actions, and determining the next step.</p>
<div id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFCCF;--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
<div id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
